vegas has all sorts of workers working  all sorts of shifts a san francisco tech  company called bolt has experimented  with a four-day work week for three  months and now it's not going back bolt  is an e-commerce checkout company it's  four day work week is meant to drive up  productivity keep employees happy and  reduce burnout the change became  permanent at the beginning of the year  it's actually not about trying to cram  five days into four days the way we  think about it is actually changing the  way we work and being more effective and  efficient during those four days so  we're taking a look at are the are there  meetings that we don't need to have can  we do work a different way are we  focused in prioritizing on the most  impactful work boltz chief people  officer jennifer christie says it's not  about policing workers in fact employee  pay stays the same if you hire the right  people who are who are focused on your  mission and are here to do the great  work that we want them to do empower  them to do it and let them let them  achieve their goals and we monitor  things by goals not ours bolt says most  of its 550 employees now work remotely  since it made the news public bolt says  it's been flooded with interest from  potential employees and says it's also  hearing from other companies who want to  learn more about the four-day work week  most local governments already work a  four-day week to cut costs john langler  live local now  and we know certain departments like  city county north las vegas they've got  that four-day work week we have a couple  former colleagues who work over there  they love it the four-day work week so  it's interesting i have a couple friends  who have that schedule they love it they  they get to work a little bit harder but  they do enjoy that extra time so of  course  not for us here in news though  thanks for staying with us here at for  remember you can join us anytime on  eightnewsnow.com the five o'clock starts  right now  you
 

